ong Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $497K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $43K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Reservoir Media, Inc.. is a small-cap communication services business with a $669M market cap on $176M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $50M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 28 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.04\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 48% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 63% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6266440390326686},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Communication Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 17% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Looking for a Growth Stock? 3 Reasons Why Reservoir Media (RSVR) is a Solid Choice","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036123/looking-for-a-growth-stock-3-reasons-why-reservoir-media-rsvr-is-a-solid-choice?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_11_growth-3036123","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795711502.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (RSVR) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/23/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_RSVR_Volatility_112626092602_1795703162.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795703162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in RSVR Response","source":"news.stocktradersdail